Z||000000||CC Rider||07-31-2001||10:58 AM||||1987 V6 Auto <BR>The other day I turned on the A/C and smoke came out of the vents on the dash. <BR>Did not smell like wire insulation but the A/C fan would not work after that. I turned it off and came back to it a few hrs later and it's like it never happened and I can't get it to do it again - not that I'd want it to but I'd like to fix it.<P>??????????<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mope||07-31-2001||11:36 AM||||if it didnt smell like anything burning it might just be like a fog, not smoke. I am no expert but my dads ford pickup used to randomly do it all the time. The AC in that truck was some of the best i had ever used.<P>mope||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||07-31-2001||12:10 PM||||If the smoke doesn't smell sweet or "rusty" (coolant) or like something's burning, it may just be due to excess humidity inside the car which the A/C is condensing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||07-31-2001||08:04 PM||||take out the heater motor resistor and check it. you get to it from the spare tire bay. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||08-01-2001||11:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>take out the heater motor resistor and check it. you get to it from the spare tire bay. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep, It gets leaves around it. It is located next to the heater blower. It has 2 7MM screws & a plug with 3 wires connected to it. It looks is a little egg shaped disk on the outside but has coils on the inside.<P><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
